{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0cd-d72e-7f30-ae43-709d74382df9"},"sequence":61,"recorded_at":1780531400000117,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0ce-0331-7622-a93c-1c1a010ef9e3"},"task_id":"01a0b0ce-0331-7622-a93c-1c1a010ef9e3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0ce-0331-7622-a93c-1c1a010ef9e3","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_producer.md`.\n1|Own TASK-260830-219okr (implement-dual-stack-major-negotiation), first leaf of STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation, EPIC M2; sibling 19bjfj follows). Landed owners you build on: internal/rpcwire (RPC 2/3/4/5 envelopes, hello maps, namespaces, contract profiles, limits, Structured Error framing statically bound per major) and internal/hostchannel (Host Channel 1.0.0 / RPC 5 authenticated endpoint) from STORY-260830-1kiyj6, plus the Config-4 selection in internal/config. Implement, as production code, major negotiation under the pinned Sections 11.2-11.3 (framing/handshake, hello as the first request, request_id echo, closed operation registry), 11.8/11.9 (RPC 3 directory-capable and RPC 4 TerminalBackend-evidence majors; a v3 node negotiating v2 performs core sync only and exposes the peer as directory_mesh_unsupported, never as zero inventory; the same shape for RPC 4 backend-evidence activation), 11.10.1 (RPC 5 on the Config-4 host channel with contracts.rpc [\"5.0.0\"] only) and 17.1-17.4 (compatibility: unsupported majors, unknown closed fields/tags fail closed; RPC 3 and 2 dual-stack for at least one stable release; legacy RPC 2/3/4 dual-stack obligations apply only to explicitly legacy installations and never require a Config-4 endpoint to accept legacy — no byte sniffing, extension field, argv value, environment value or failed handshake can select a fallback; Section 6.6): a negotiator that, given the local installation's configuration generation and the peer's hello, selects exactly one common major or refuses no-common-major with the pinned Section 15 class (incompatible_protocol, exit 6, only when incompatibility is actually known), preserves core-only peers (RPC 2 core sync, unsupported directory/backend activation exposed explicitly as directory_mesh_unsupported / the RPC 4 equivalent, never as zero inventory or a capability claim), never downgrades a Config-4 host-channel endpoint below RPC 5 and never substitutes negotiation for the hostchannel admission (identity equality, allowlist, generation) that TASK-260830-z1yxg9 owns; for explicitly legacy installations select the highest common major among 2/3/4 with the exact per-major contract keys (RPC 2: 14 contracts/6 namespaces; RPC 3: 24 keys/7 namespaces; RPC 4: 25 keys/8 namespaces; RPC 5: RPC 4 shapes with protocol_version 5.0.0) and the historically bound Structured Error version per major; refuse a v2 bound inside a v3+ frame and any cross-major mixing. Tests: drive the negotiator with every pair (local majors × peer hello majors) as a table derived from the pinned text, positives for each admitted selection, negatives for no-common-major, mixed-major frames, a Config-4 endpoint offered legacy, a legacy installation offered RPC 5 only, sniffing/fallback attempts (byte sniffing, extension field, argv, env, failed handshake), and the core-only exposure invariant (a core-only peer's inventory is reported as unsupported activation, not empty); every gate a narrowing mutant; the peer-visible outcomes must be pure data (no capability advertised).\n2|COMMON CONTRACT (first leaf of a Story on trunk 7efe385 or later). Normative authority: the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md headings named below; the v0.7.0 adoption (STORY-260916-3uqbwq) is landing during your run and is byte-identical in these sections — if it has landed when you refresh, cite SPEC.v0.7.0.md with the same heading numbers. Reuse the landed owners (canonicaljson closed shapes, scalar, sessrepo/sessstate/sessquery, sessckpt, matjournal, crashgate, fencing, sessprofile, provhost/resumesmoke, hosttrust/peeridentity/sshtransport, rpcwire/hostchannel, sessadapter, terminalbackend, localstore, secprim/secconftest) — never fork a second model; extend or adopt. Traceability: do NOT edit internal/traceability (ownership registry, digest pin, README measured-coverage subsection) in this first leaf — the Story's FINAL leaf carries the registry bindings and re-pin once the v0.7.0 registry is on trunk; document your clause coverage in a package-local TRACEABILITY.md and the conformance matrix instead. Evidence contract (repository DoD): every AC row driven through a production entry by a named committed test with a stated n-of-m ratio and call sites; negatives for every refusal; a narrowing mutant per gate executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__); crash/idempotency evidence for every durable write (landed no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern) or an explicit purity bound; conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to a test or a stated bound; README package section with test commands and NO capability/CLI claim (no ax command exists); LOGBOOK entry newest-first. Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-4qojoz/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-4qojoz forked from current trunk; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED; never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if origin/main moves before your handoff run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-219okr` (LOGBOOK append conflicts are resolved with --replay-resolutions: copy the retained resolution-template.json header and add {\"checkpoint_oid\": <REBASE_HEAD original checkpoint>, \"path\": \"LOGBOOK.md\", \"sha256\": <hex of the full replacement>, \"content\": <base64>} keeping every entry newest-first), then audit every path in `git diff --name-only <old-base> <new-base>` that appears in your git status and restore trunk content by hand (README/LOGBOOK purely additive; task-board.config.json == HEAD); before handoff `git status` shows only candidate paths. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured 26-command validation suite once before handoff (command 21 is `cataloggen -adopted … -check`); hand off no later than 3.5 hours in — if the full scope cannot be finished, hand off a reviewable slice with the remaining items enumerated precisely in the results. Attach TASK-260830-219okr_results.md, TASK-260830-219okr_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-219okr_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-219okr --role developer` and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be claude-opus-5 max.","final_result":true}}}
