ackendEvidenceUnsupportedCode`, so the expectation is derived from the implementation itself: the literal `directory_mesh_unsupported` appears in committed tests only inside a comment and `terminal_backend_unavailable` appears nowhere. The reviewer's plants R19 (swap to `continuation_route_unavailable`, same exit 6) and R20 (swap to `terminal_backend_capability_unproven`, same exit 6) both SURVIVED the committed suite twice — a core-only peer could be exposed under any registered exit-6 code of the bound version and AC rows 3 and 4 would still read PASS. Fix: assert the LITERAL Section 11.8 token and the chosen RPC-4 token at the production entry (`Negotiate(...).Peer.Directory.Code == \"directory_mesh_unsupported\"`, `...Peer.BackendEvidence.Code == \"terminal_backend_unavailable\"`), and add both same-exit swap plants to `mutations.py` naming those tests as their killers.\n4|F2 (P2) — the Section 6.6 unknown-generation refusal is pinned only at the helper. Conformance row 5 credits `TestLocalMajors unknown-*`, which calls `LocalMajors` directly; no committed test drives `Negotiate` with an unknown generation and asserts the class (`TestNegotiateMatrix` uses the four known generations; `TestNegotiationIsDeterministic` includes \"9.9.9\" but only compares outputs to themselves). The reviewer's plant R12 — on `LocalMajors` refusal, fall back to `local = []int{2,3,4}` instead of returning, exactly the \"unknown configuration … never legacy selection\" violation 6.6 forbids — SURVIVED twice. Fix: drive `Negotiate` with unknown generations (\"\", \"5.0.0\", \"9.9.9\", \"4.0.1\" and at least one more) crossed with every pinned frame, asserting code, exit, reason, sentinel and a zero `Decision{}`; add a Negotiate-site narrowing plant to `mutations.py`.\n5|F3 (P2) — the documented generation input names the wrong production field. negotiate.go:170-172 and :449-450 name `config.Configuration.SchemaVersion`, but the landed config owner normalizes it: `translateCommon` sets `SchemaVersion: CurrentVersion` (\"3.0.0\") for every v1/v2/v3 source and only `translateV4` overrides it, so the source generation is `LoadedConfiguration.SourceVersion`. The reviewer proved it with `config.Decode` on minimal v1/v2/v3 documents: source 1.0.0 gives `Value.SchemaVersion=3.0.0` -> `LocalMajors=[2 3 4]` while `SourceVersion=1.0.0` gives `[2]`. A wiring leaf following the current doc would make a Config-1/2 installation offer RPC 3/4 it has no directory or backend tables for — the zero-inventory appearance 11.8 forbids. Fix: document `LoadedConfiguration.SourceVersion` (or take the generation as an explicit type so the wrong field cannot be passed), and pin the `LocalMajors` vocabulary against `config.Version1/Version2/CurrentVersion/Version4` in a test so the two owners cannot drift silently.\n6|F4 (P3) — `PeerOffer` re-validates the key set and the `rpc` array only; a directly built v3/v4/v5 hello with `session_event=[\"1.0.0\"]`, or a v2 hello with `lease=[\"9.9.9\"]`, is admitted (the composed production path closes the hole because `Request.Hello()`/`Response.Hello()` are the only production constructors, so this is a bound, not a production defect) — but the committed comment \"PeerOffer must re-validate every negotiation-relevant member for direct callers\" over-claims. Either state the bound explicitly in the doc comment, README and TRACEABILITY, or add the full per-key comparison for v3+ frames plus per-key 1-16 sorted-unique semver for v2. Pick one and say which.\n7|F5 (P3) — the frame-vocabulary gate is measured only at the 2.x/3.x edges; the plant admitting \"5.1.0\" into `pinnedFrameVersions` survived twice (downstream still fails closed, but the refusal degrades from `incompatible_protocol`/6 to an unclassified internal error). Add `4.1.0`, `5.0.1` and `5.1.0` rows and a 5.x-edge plant. For unparseable strings (\"\", \"garbage\", \"v2.0.0\") the gate answers `incompatible_protocol`/6 while Section 15.1 assigns `transport_failure` to an unrecognizable version; it is unreachable through rpcwire decode, so a stated bound is enough — write it down.\n8|F6 (P3) — the TRACEABILITY 17.1 row credits \"highest mutually supported minor within a common major\" to `Select` while the same file lists within-major minor selection as a stated bound; drop the minor clause from the covered row.\n9|Procedure: the managed Story worktree .temp/STORY-260830-4qojoz/worktree (branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-4qojoz) holds your uncommitted candidate on base 888ae3d, which is current origin/main — do not refresh unless origin/main actually moves; if it does, run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-219okr`, then audit every path in `git diff --name-only 888ae3d <new base>` that also appears in your `git status` and restore trunk content by hand (README/LOGBOOK purely additive; task-board.config.json byte-identical to the new base). Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Re-run the full configured 27-command validation suite once (command 5 `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs — expected, do not shorten it), update TASK-260830-219okr_results.md with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test or plant that fails without it -> evidence path), update TASK-260830-219okr_conformance-matrix.md (row 5 is the one credited to a helper call; rows 3 and 4 are the circular ones) and TASK-260830-219okr_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive with one raw log per plant and its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__), reset and re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-219okr --role developer` so revision 4 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 2.5 hours in — this rework is small. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 4.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
