{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c66f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0cd-d72e-7f30-ae43-709d74382df9"},"sequence":402,"recorded_at":1780531400000799,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0ce-a156-7a21-adcd-171fc9e2313a"},"task_id":"01a0b0ce-a156-7a21-adcd-171fc9e2313a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0ce-a156-7a21-adcd-171fc9e2313a","chunk":"Read text file `.temp/resources/TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_review-verdict-rev3.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-219okr review verdict — Change Request revision 3\n2|\n3|- Reviewer run: RUN-260917-92b548 (reviewer/reviewer, claude-opus-5 max)\n4|- Candidate: CR-TASK-260830-219okr-3, base `888ae3dff6a55c29bfaf311957748d405ed1ab06`, tree `a9d0ffe9fa05df312554aa181134e8a623d42375`, 8 changed paths; patch sha256 `67bbeede…cc78c0` re-derived (`git diff --binary base..tree` byte-equal to the attached patch); working tree == candidate tree (temporary index `write-tree`); `origin/main` == base at review time.\n5|- Method: isolated immutable copy (`git archive` of the candidate tree under `.temp/TASK-260830-219okr/review/candidate`), overlay-only mutants, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; the live Story worktree, index, branch and HEAD were never mutated. Evidence archive: `TASK-260830-219okr_review-evidence-rev3.tar.gz`.\n6|\n7|## Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED → `to-dev`\n8|\n9|`repeat-of: none` (revisions 1 and 2 carried no review findings).\n10|\n11|Production behavior matched every pinned rule I drove (32 pair rows, 32 hostile offers, exposure, no-fallback, purity). The rejection is on the evidence and the documented integration contract: two AC-named outcomes are pinned circularly or only at a helper, so narrowing/class-swap plants at the production entry survive the committed suite (4 survivors, each reproduced twice, each killed by a reviewer probe), and the documented generation input names a field the landed config owner normalizes away. Fixes are small (tests, one harness row set, doc comment); no production selection logic needs to change for F1/F2.\n12|\n13|## Findings\n14|\n15|### F1 — P2 — AC exposure tokens pinned circularly; same-exit code swaps survive\n16|- Shape: expectation derived from the implementation's own table (`references/negative-evidence.md`, \"Derive Completeness From An Independent Source\").\n17|- `TestPeerExposure` (conformance_test.go:34-45) and `TestRefusalClassesResolveFromTheRegistry` (:149-150) compare `Decision.Peer.*.Code` against `meshneg.DirectoryUnsupportedCode` / `meshneg.BackendEvidenceUnsupportedCode`, i.e. the production constants. The literal `directory_mesh_unsupported` occurs in committed tests only inside a comment; `terminal_backend_unavailable` occurs nowhere in committed tests.\n18|- Plants (negotiate.go:56 / :62): `R19` swap `directory_mesh_unsupported` → `continuation_route_unavailable` (also 1.2.0/exit 6); `R20` swap `terminal_backend_unavailable` → `terminal_backend_capability_unproven` (also 1.3.0/exit 6). Both SURVIVED the committed suite twice (15/15 top-level PASS, exit 0) and were KILLED by the reviewer literal pin (`TestReviewPairTable`). A core-only peer could be exposed under any registered exit-6 code of the bound version and AC rows 3/4 would still read PASS.\n19|- Fix: assert the literal Section 11.8 token and the chosen RPC-4 token at the production entry (`Negotiate(...).Peer.Directory.Code == \"directory_mesh_unsupported\"`, `...BackendEvidence.Code == \"terminal_backend_unavailable\"`), and add the two same-exit swap plants to `mutations.py` with those named killers.\n20|\n21|### F2 — P2 — Section 6.6 unknown-generation refusal pinned only at the helper; the production entry can fall back to legacy unnoticed\n22|- Shape: check present but pinned by direct helper call, not through the composed path (`negative-evidence.md`, TASK-260730-2c1e8l cycle 2).\n23|- The conformance matrix row 5 credits `TestLocalMajors unknown-*`, which calls `LocalMajors` directly. No committed test drives `Negotiate` with an unknown generation and asserts the class: `TestNegotiateMatrix` uses the four known generations; `TestNegotiationIsDeterministic` includes \"9.9.9\" but only compares outputs to themselves.\n24|- Plant `R12` (negotiate.go:467-470): on `LocalMajors` refusal, `local = []int{2, 3, 4}` instead of returning — exactly the \"unknown configuration … never legacy selection\" violation Section 6.6 forbids. SURVIVED the committed suite twice; KILLED by `TestReviewPairTable` (unknown-generation rows expect `invalid_config`/3/`ReasonUnknownConfig` and a zero `Decision`).\n25|- Fix: drive `Negotiate` with unknown generations (`\"\"`, `\"5.0.0\"`, `\"9.9.9\"`, `\"4.0.1\"`, …) × every pinned frame in `TestNegotiateMatrix` (or a sibling), asserting code/exit/reason/sentinel and `Decision{}`; add a Negotiate-site narrowing plant to `mutations.py`.\n26|\n27|### F3 — P2 — Documented generation input is the wrong production field\n28|- negotiate.go:170-172 and :449-450 name `config.Configuration.SchemaVersion` as the generation input. The landed owner normalizes it: `translateCommon` sets `SchemaVersion: CurrentVersion` (\"3.0.0\") for every v1/v2/v3 source (internal/config/validation.go:193; schema.go:55-56 \"Value always has SchemaVersion CurrentVersion\"), and only `translateV4` overrides to \"4.0.0\" (validation.go:141). The source generation is `LoadedConfiguration.SourceVersion`.\n29|- Proven with `config.Decode` on minimal v1/v2/v3 documents (log `review-config-probe.log`): source 1.0.0 → `Value.SchemaVersion=3.0.0` → `LocalMajors=[2 3 4]`, while `SourceVersion=1.0.0` → `[2]`; source 2.0.0 → `[2 3 4]` vs `[2 3]`.\n30|- Consequence: a wiring leaf following this doc makes a Config-1/2 installation offer RPC 3/4 it has no directory/backend tables for — the zero-inventory appearance 11.8 forbids, and a departure from the mapping this leaf claims (Config-1 → [2], Config-2 → [2,3]). The Config-4 no-downgrade rule is unaffected (v4 stays distinguishable).\n31|- Fix: document `LoadedConfiguration.SourceVersion` (or take the generation as an explicit type), and pin the `LocalMajors` vocabulary against `config.Version1/Version2/CurrentVersion/Version4` in a test so the two owners cannot drift silently.\n32|\n33|### F4 — P3 — `PeerOffer` re-validates keys and the `rpc` array only; non-`rpc` array values are trusted from decode\n34|- 11.8/11.9 require exact values for every key of the v3/v4/v5 map (\"a different version … fails incompatible_protocol\"); `PeerOffer` checks key count/membership and the `rpc` array, not the other arrays. Probe: a v3/v4/v5 hello with `session_event=[\"1.0.0\"]`, and a v2 hello with `lease=[\"9.9.9\"]`, built directly, are ADMITTED by `PeerOffer` (returns the framing major); the same hellos are refused by `rpcwire` decode (`incompatible RPC hello structure`).\n35|- Through the composed production path (`Request.Hello()`/`Response.Hello()` are the only production constructors) the hole is closed, so this is a stated-bound defect, not a production one — but the committed test comment \"PeerOffer must re-validate every negotiation-relevant member for direct callers\" over-claims. Either state the bound (README/TRACEABILITY/doc: non-`rpc` arrays are validated by rpcwire decode and trusted here) or add `maps.EqualFunc(hello.Contracts, profile, slices.Equal)` for v3+ frames (and per-key 1–16 sorted-unique semver for v2), which is a few lines.\n36|\n37|### F5 — P3 — Frame-vocabulary gate measured only at the 2.x/3.x edges; unparseable-version class differs from 15.1\n38|- `TestPeerOfferRefusals/frame-versions` probes `2.1.0` and `3.0.1`; plant `R8` admitting `\"5.1.0\"` into `pinnedFrameVersions` SURVIVED twice (the downstream `rpcwire.ContractProfile` still fails closed, so no selection results, but the refusal degrades from `incompatible_protocol`/6 to an unclassified internal error). Add `4.1.0`/`5.0.1`/`5.1.0` rows and a 5.x-edge plant.\n39|- For unparseable strings (`\"\"`, `\"garbage\"`, `\"v2.0.0\"`) the gate answers `incompatible_protocol`/6, whereas 15.1 assigns `transport_failure` to an unrecognizable version; unreachable via rpcwire decode (only the four pinned strings decode), so a stated bound suffices.\n40|\n41|### F6 — P3 — TRACEABILITY wording\n42|- The 17.1 row credits \"highest mutually supported minor within a common major\" to `Select` while the same file lists within-major minor selection as a stated bound; drop the minor clause from the covered row.\n43|\n44|## Verified (reviewer instruments; all logs in the evidence archive)\n45|\n46|1. Spec fidelity (SPEC.v0.6.0.md sha256 `74504539…896b` == `specpin.DocumentSHA256V060`): generation→majors mapping, unknown→`invalid_config`/3, per-major key sets and namespaces (rpcwire profiles diffed against the spec's literal JSON blocks: 14/24/25/25 keys, values equal; namespaces 6/7/8/8), Error bindings 1.0.0/1.2.0/1.3.0/1.3.0 via `axerror.BindingFor`, v2 map inside a v3+ frame refused, core-only exposure derived from the selected major, no-fallback surface — all match negotiate.go. Binding choice `terminal_backend_unavailable`: 11.9 names no code; 17.4 says \"report activation unavailable\"; 15.3 (1.3.0 exit-6 row) registers exactly that token; 11.10.1/15.3 forbid minting — defensible, and `internal/axerror` is untouched by the CR (no code minted). Refusing a multi-major `rpc` array inside one frame is not a literal clause; it follows 17.1 (\"MUST NOT select a major by coercion\") and the task brief's \"refuse … any cross-major mixing\".\n47|2. Pair table: 32 rows driven through `Negotiate` (16 known-generation pairs: highest common == the peer's framing major or `incompatible_protocol`/6/`no_common_major` with Local/Peer facts; 16 unknown-generation pairs: `invalid_config`/3). 32 hostile offers (v3 frame with 14-key map, v2 frame with 24 keys, v5 frame with 24 keys, v5 frame with the v4 map, v4 frame with the v5 map, unsorted, duplicate, multi-major 2+3 / 2..5 / 4+5-in-v5, 6.0.0 frames, rpc 6.0.0 in v5, 5.0.0→Config-3, legacy 2/3/4→Config-4, extension/fallback-hint/error/host_channel/substituted/missing-rpc keys, nil contracts, zero hello, 5.1.0/prerelease/range rpc, v-prefix, huge major, 17 entries) all refused with the exact reason/class/exit, zero `Decision`, exits re-derived from `axerror.ExitCodeFor(1.0.0, …)`.\n48|3. Core-only exposure: Config-2/3 × v2 → `directory_mesh_unsupported`/6 and `terminal_backend_unavailable`/6; Config-3 × v3 → directory negotiated, backend unsupported. Structural pin reddens when `FeatureActivation` gains `Inventory int` (R16) or `PeerView` gains `Count int` (R17) — both KILLED by `TestExposureCarriesNoInventory`.\n49|4. Separation from admission: `internal/meshneg` has no production importer; `internal/hostchannel` does not import it and every exported hostchannel entry takes typed `hosttrust`/`config`/`tls`/`Stream` inputs (no `any`), so a `Decision` cannot be presented as an admission token. Config-4 cannot be talked below RPC 5 by any frame, map, env (`AX_RPC_MAJOR=2`, `AX_ALLOW_LEGACY=1`), argv (`--legacy --rpc-major=2`) or three failed attempts followed by a valid RPC 5 offer.\n50|5. Purity: direct import census exact (`errors fmt regexp slices strconv strings` + `axerror rpcwire`); the four consulted owner functions are pure lookups; the transitive closure does reach `os/io/net/time/crypto/rand/os/exec` through owners (rpcwire→sshtransport, axerror→catalog), which the README correctly scopes to \"direct imports\". Stated crash/idempotency bound accepted; `TestNegotiationIsDeterministic` holds.\n51|6. Mutation: producer harness re-executed twice in the isolated copy — 29 probes = 27 narrowing KILLED (each by its named test), neutral passed, `detail-text` control SURVIVED, exit 0, no `__pycache__`, results identical to the producer's `results.json`. Reviewer plants (17 rows, `review_mutants.py`): 12 KILLED by the named committed test (R1 duplicate admitted `>=`→`>`; R2 Negotiate widens the peer set with 5; R3 Select admits 5 without the peer; R4 any extra key; R5 negotiated feature carries a code; R6 v5 inexact rpc exempt; R7 refusal code swap same exit; R9 unknown 4.0.1; R13 Negotiate trusts the frame on a malformed offer; R16/R17 structural; R18 invalid_config same-exit swap), 4 SURVIVED (R8, R12, R19, R20 — F5/F2/F1/F1), control C1 survived. Of the brief's four suggested arms: highest→lowest (producer `select-picks-lowest`), Config-4 admits 4 (producer `config4-admits-4`, reviewer R2/R3), duplicate accepted (reviewer R1 — the producer's `mixed-admits-unsorted-pair` narrows only the descending pair), key count off by one (producer `shape-admits-extra-key`, reviewer R4) — all killed.\n52|7. Docs/hygiene: root README delta is 16 additive lines inside \"Mesh RPC envelopes and Host Channel\", no capability/CLI claim, measured-coverage subsection untouched; LOGBOOK delta 8 additive lines, newest-first (the duplicated `## 2026-09-17` headers lower in the file pre-exist on trunk); `internal/traceability` and `internal/axerror` untouched; `task-board.config.json` == HEAD; changed paths exactly the 8 candidate paths; no `__pycache__`/`.pyc`; gofmt whole tree clean; `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` exit 0; `tracecheck` exit 0; `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` exit 0 on the exact tree; `go test ./internal/meshneg ./internal/rpcwire ./internal/hostchannel -count=1` ok and `-race` ok; meshneg `-race -cover` 87.8%. Accepted from the runtime's bounded CR validation log (not rerun here): full `go test ./...` verbose/race/cover, 14 fuzz smokes, cross-builds, JSON census, `task-board validate`, `git diff --check` — final line `required=27 green=27 failed=0 missing=0`.\n53|\n54|## Checklist routing\n55|Producer items 7 (\"driven through the production entry point…\") and 9 (\"every gate ships a narrowing mutant…\") are unchecked for F1/F2; reviewer items \"Solution fits project architecture\", \"Tests green\", \"Gate … attacked, not read\" and \"verdict evidence added and status routed\" are checked; \"Implementation matches AC\" stays unchecked pending F1–F3. Status → `to-dev`.","final_result":true}}}
