lassified internal error). Add `4.1.0`/`5.0.1`/`5.1.0` rows and a 5.x-edge plant.\n39|- For unparseable strings (`\"\"`, `\"garbage\"`, `\"v2.0.0\"`) the gate answers `incompatible_protocol`/6, whereas 15.1 assigns `transport_failure` to an unrecognizable version; unreachable via rpcwire decode (only the four pinned strings decode), so a stated bound suffices.\n40|\n41|### F6 — P3 — TRACEABILITY wording\n42|- The 17.1 row credits \"highest mutually supported minor within a common major\" to `Select` while the same file lists within-major minor selection as a stated bound; drop the minor clause from the covered row.\n43|\n44|## Verified (reviewer instruments; all logs in the evidence archive)\n45|\n46|1. Spec fidelity (SPEC.v0.6.0.md sha256 `74504539…896b` == `specpin.DocumentSHA256V060`): generation→majors mapping, unknown→`invalid_config`/3, per-major key sets and namespaces (rpcwire profiles diffed against the spec's literal JSON blocks: 14/24/25/25 keys, values equal; namespaces 6/7/8/8), Error bindings 1.0.0/1.2.0/1.3.0/1.3.0 via `axerror.BindingFor`, v2 map inside a v3+ frame refused, core-only exposure derived from the selected major, no-fallback surface — all match negotiate.go. Binding choice `terminal_backend_unavailable`: 11.9 names no code; 17.4 says \"report activation unavailable\"; 15.3 (1.3.0 exit-6 row) registers exactly that token; 11.10.1/15.3 forbid minting — defensible, and `internal/axerror` is untouched by the CR (no code minted). Refusing a multi-major `rpc` array inside one frame is not a literal clause; it follows 17.1 (\"MUST NOT select a major by coercion\") and the task brief's \"refuse … any cross-major mixing\".\n47|2. Pair table: 32 rows driven through `Negotiate` (16 known-generation pairs: highest common == the peer's framing major or `incompatible_protocol`/6/`no_common_major` with Local/Peer facts; 16 unknown-generation pairs: `invalid_config`/3). 32 hostile offers (v3 frame with 14-key map, v2 frame with 24 keys, v5 frame with 24 keys, v5 frame with the v4 map, v4 frame with the v5 map, unsorted, duplicate, multi-major 2+3 / 2..5 / 4+5-in-v5, 6.0.0 frames, rpc 6.0.0 in v5, 5.0.0→Config-3, legacy 2/3/4→Config-4, extension/fallback-hint/error/host_channel/substituted/missing-rpc keys, nil contracts, zero hello, 5.1.0/prerelease/range rpc, v-prefix, huge major, 17 entries) all refused with the exact reason/class/exit, zero `Decision`, exits re-derived from `axerror.ExitCodeFor(1.0.0, …)`.\n48|3. Core-only exposure: Config-2/3 × v2 → `directory_mesh_unsupported`/6 and `terminal_backend_unavailable`/6; Config-3 × v3 → directory negotiated, backend unsupported. Structural pin reddens when `FeatureActivation` gains `Inventory int` (R16) or `PeerView` gains `Count int` (R17) — both KILLED by `TestExposureCarriesNoInventory`.\n49|4. Separation from admission: `internal/meshneg` has no production importer; `internal/hostchannel` does not import it and every exported hostchannel entry takes typed `hosttrust`/`config`/`tls`/`Stream` inputs (no `any`), so a `Decision` cannot be presented as an admission token. Config-4 cannot be talked below RPC 5 by any frame, map, env (`AX_RPC_MAJOR=2`, `AX_ALLOW_LEGACY=1`), argv (`--legacy --rpc-major=2`) or three failed attempts followed by a valid RPC 5 offer.\n50|5. Purity: direct import census exact (`errors fmt regexp slices strconv strings` + `axerror rpcwire`); the four consulted owner functions are pure lookups; the transitive closure does reach `os/io/net/time/crypto/rand/os/exec` through owners (rpcwire→sshtransport, axerror→catalog), which the README correctly scopes to \"direct imports\". Stated crash/idempotency bound accepted; `TestNegotiationIsDeterministic` holds.\n51|6. Mutation: producer harness re-executed twice in the isolated copy — 29 probes = 27 narrowing KILLED (each by its named test), neutral passed, `detail-text` control SURVIVED, exit 0, no `__pycache__`, results identical to the producer's `results.json`. Reviewer plants (17 rows, `review_mutants.py`): 12 KILLED by the named committed test (R1 duplicate admitted `>=`→`>`; R2 Negotiate widens the peer set with 5; R3 Select admits 5 without the peer; R4 any extra key; R5 negotiated feature carries a code; R6 v5 inexact rpc exempt; R7 refusal code swap same exit; R9 unknown 4.0.1; R13 Negotiate trusts the frame on a malformed offer; R16/R17 structural; R18 invalid_config same-exit swap), 4 SURVIVED (R8, R12, R19, R20 — F5/F2/F1/F1), control C1 survived. Of the brief's four suggested arms: highest→lowest (producer `select-picks-lowest`), Config-4 admits 4 (producer `config4-admits-4`, reviewer R2/R3), duplicate accepted (reviewer R1 — the producer's `mixed-admits-unsorted-pair` narrows only the descending pair), key count off by one (producer `shape-admits-extra-key`, reviewer R4) — all killed.\n52|7. Docs/hygiene: root README delta is 16 additive lines inside \"Mesh RPC envelopes and Host Channel\", no capability/CLI claim, measured-coverage subsection untouched; LOGBOOK delta 8 additive lines, newest-first (the duplicated `## 2026-09-17` headers lower in the file pre-exist on trunk); `internal/traceability` and `internal/axerror` untouched; `task-board.config.json` == HEAD; changed paths exactly the 8 candidate paths; no `__pycache__`/`.pyc`; gofmt whole tree clean; `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` exit 0; `tracecheck` exit 0; `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` exit 0 on the exact tree; `go test ./internal/meshneg ./internal/rpcwire ./internal/hostchannel -count=1` ok and `-race` ok; meshneg `-race -cover` 87.8%. Accepted from the runtime's bounded CR validation log (not rerun here): full `go test ./...` verbose/race/cover, 14 fuzz smokes, cross-builds, JSON census, `task-board validate`, `git diff --check` — final line `required=27 green=27 failed=0 missing=0`.\n53|\n54|## Checklist routing\n55|Producer items 7 (\"driven through the production entry point…\") and 9 (\"every gate ships a narrowing mutant…\") are unchecked for F1/F2; reviewer items \"Solution fits project architecture\", \"Tests green\", \"Gate … attacked, not read\" and \"verdict evidence added and status routed\" are checked; \"Implementation matches AC\" stays unchecked pending F1–F3. Status → `to-dev`.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
