{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c757","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0cd-d72e-7f30-ae43-709d74382df9"},"sequence":518,"recorded_at":1780531400001031,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0ce-dddb-7862-9ccd-a23756accf93"},"task_id":"01a0b0ce-dddb-7862-9ccd-a23756accf93","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0ce-dddb-7862-9ccd-a23756accf93","chunk":"Read text file `internal/meshneg/README.md`.\n1|# Mesh RPC major negotiation\n2|\n3|Owner: TASK-260830-219okr in STORY-260830-4qojoz. Authority: embedded AX\n4|v0.6.0 SPEC.md, commit `0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`,\n5|Sections 11.2-11.3, 11.8, 11.9, 11.10.1, 15.1-15.3, 17.1-17.4, and 6.6.\n6|\n7|`Negotiate` selects exactly one common Mesh RPC major from the local\n8|installation's configuration generation and the peer's decoded hello frame.\n9|Config-4 installations offer exactly RPC 5; explicitly legacy installations\n10|offer the historical dual-stack sets (Config-1: 2; Config-2: 2 and 3;\n11|Config-3: 2, 3, and 4). The peer offer must be single-major and agree with\n12|its framing major; any mixing is refused rather than coerced. A disjoint\n13|pair is refused as no-common-major with the pinned `incompatible_protocol`\n14|class (exit 6), and only from actually known inputs: unframed bytes never\n15|reach this package.\n16|\n17|A selection carries the exact pinned shapes for its major (contracts map,\n18|namespace vocabulary, statically bound Structured Error version), rebuilt\n19|from the landed owners rather than copied from peer bytes, plus the peer\n20|exposure: above-core activation the selection does not carry is reported as\n21|explicitly unsupported (`directory_mesh_unsupported`, or the RPC-4\n22|equivalent `terminal_backend_unavailable`), never as zero inventory. Every\n23|outcome is pure data: no wire bytes are framed, no connection is opened, no\n24|capability is advertised, and no admission decision is made. Identity\n25|equality, allowlist membership, and trust generation remain the\n26|`internal/hostchannel` boundary owned by TASK-260830-z1yxg9.\n27|\n28|## Implemented surface and traceability\n29|\n30|| Pinned rule | Production call site | Named test | Bound |\n31|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n32|| 6.4/6.5/6.6 generation to offered majors; 11.8/11.9 dual-stack; 11.10.1 RPC 5 only | LocalMajors | TestLocalMajors, TestNegotiateMatrix | Unknown generation refuses invalid_config/3, never legacy selection |\n33|| 11.2/11.8/11.9/11.10.1 exact per-major contracts; 17.1 no coercion | PeerOffer | TestPeerOfferRefusals, TestSemverAgreementWithRPCWire | v2 1-16 minor ranges negotiate the major; within-major minor selection stays future work |\n34|| Highest common major; 17.2 reader rules | Select | TestSelectHighestCommon | Inputs outside 2/3/4/5 refuse even beside a common pinned major |\n35|| No-common-major refusal, known only; 15.1-15.3 class | Negotiate -> Refusal | TestNegotiateMatrix, TestRefusalShape, TestRefusalClassesResolveFromTheRegistry | Frames nothing; the initiator maps the class to its local error |\n36|| 11.8/11.9 core-only preservation; unsupported activation, never zero inventory | Negotiate -> Decision.Peer | TestPeerExposure, TestExposureCarriesNoInventory | Exposure derives from the negotiated major alone |\n37|| 6.6 no downgrade of Config-4; legacy never coerces RPC 5 | LocalMajors, Negotiate | TestConfig4NeverDowngrades, TestLegacyNeverSelectsRPC5 | Config-4 offers exactly [5] |\n38|| 11.10.1 admission separation (identity, allowlist, generation) | Negotiate (ignores them) | TestNegotiationIsNotAdmission | Admission still required before dispatch |\n39|| 6.6 no sniffing/extension/argv/env/handshake fallback | Negotiate (no such input) | TestNoFallbackSurface | Pure function; statelessness and determinism pinned by test |\n40|| 11.2/11.8/11.9/11.10.1 shapes; 15.1/15.3/11.10.1 error bindings | decisionFor via rpcwire, axerror | TestDecisionShapes | Shapes rebuilt from profiles, never copied from the peer |\n41|\n42|**11 of 11 AC rows are driven through the production entries by named\n43|tests** (matrix in `TASK-260830-219okr_conformance-matrix.md`): common-major\n44|selection, core-only preservation, directory exposure, backend exposure,\n45|no-common-major refusal, Config-4 no-downgrade, admission separation,\n46|cross-major refusal, no-fallback surface, exact per-major shapes with bound\n47|error versions, and pure-data outcomes.\n48|\n49|The package performs no I/O and keeps no state. Its direct imports are\n50|`errors`, `fmt`, `regexp`, `slices`, `strconv`, `strings` plus the `rpcwire`\n51|and `axerror` owners (no `os`, `io`, `net`, `time`, `rand`, or `exec`), and\n52|the owners are consulted through pure functions only (`ContractProfile`,\n53|`Namespaces`, `ExitCodeFor`, `BindingFor`), so there is no crash or\n54|idempotency surface. Determinism over the full input space is pinned by\n55|`TestNegotiationIsDeterministic`.\n56|\n57|## Checks\n58|\n59|```bash\n60|go test ./internal/meshneg -count=1 -v\n61|go test ./internal/meshneg -race -count=1 -cover\n62|PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/meshneg/mutations.py --output .temp/TASK-260830-219okr/mutations-meshneg\n63|```\n64|\n65|The mutant harness applies 27 narrowing plants plus a neutral control and\n66|one harmless applied SURVIVED control; every narrowing plant is killed by\n67|its named test with per-plant raw logs, and source originals remain\n68|untouched (overlay run).","final_result":true}}}
