{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c793","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0cd-d72e-7f30-ae43-709d74382df9"},"sequence":548,"recorded_at":1780531400001091,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0ce-ed24-7ea3-a651-e26eb68944fa"},"task_id":"01a0b0ce-ed24-7ea3-a651-e26eb68944fa","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0ce-ed24-7ea3-a651-e26eb68944fa","chunk":"Read text file `.temp/resources/TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-219okr results — implement-dual-stack-major-negotiation\n2|\n3|Role: developer. Status: ready for review (candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree).\n4|\n5|## Deliverable\n6|\n7|`internal/meshneg` (`negotiate.go`, ~470 lines): pure-data major negotiation for Mesh RPC.\n8|\n9|- `LocalMajors(configVersion)` — generation to offered majors: Config-1 → `[2]`,\n10|  Config-2 → `[2 3]`, Config-3 → `[2 3 4]`, Config-4 → exactly `[5]`; unknown\n11|  generations refuse `invalid_config`/exit 3 (Section 6.6: unknown configuration is\n12|  a refusal, never legacy selection).\n13|- `PeerOffer(frameVersion, hello)` — validates the decoded peer frame: pinned\n14|  vocabulary 2.0.0–5.0.0, exact per-major contracts keys (a v2 14-key bound inside a\n15|  v3+ frame refuses), single-major strictly sorted-unique semver rpc array agreeing\n16|  with the framing major. Any mixing refuses `incompatible_protocol`/exit 6.\n17|- `Select(local, peer)` — highest common major; inputs outside 2/3/4/5 or disjoint\n18|  pairs refuse `incompatible_protocol`/exit 6.\n19|- `Negotiate(configVersion, frameVersion, hello)` — production entry returning\n20|  `Decision` (major, protocol version, exact contracts map, namespace vocabulary,\n21|  statically bound Structured Error version, peer exposure) or `*Refusal` (pinned\n22|  Section 15 class + reason + offer facts). Frames nothing: Sections 11.2/15.1/11.10.1\n23|  close without a peer frame on unsupported majors; the initiator maps the class\n24|  to its own local error.\n25|- Core-only preservation: `Decision.Peer` reports directory activation as\n26|  `directory_mesh_unsupported` and backend-evidence activation as\n27|  `terminal_backend_unavailable` (registered exit-6 codes; exits resolved via\n28|  `axerror.ExitCodeFor`), never as zero inventory. No count/inventory member exists\n29|  in the view (structurally pinned by test).\n30|\n31|## AC coverage: 11 of 11 rows driven\n32|\n33|See `TASK-260830-219okr_conformance-matrix.md` for the row-by-row call sites and\n34|named tests (matrix rev2 stands verbatim; no production line changed since).\n35|Every refusal gate has negative tests plus at least one narrowing mutant.\n36|\n37|## Files changed (UNCOMMITTED, Story worktree only)\n38|\n39|- `internal/meshneg/negotiate.go` (new, production)\n40|- `internal/meshneg/negotiate_test.go`, `internal/meshneg/conformance_test.go` (new, tests)\n41|- `internal/meshneg/mutations.py` (new, shipped mutant harness)\n42|- `internal/meshneg/README.md`, `internal/meshneg/TRACEABILITY.md` (new, docs)\n43|- `README.md` (Mesh RPC section: paragraph + 3 tool rows; measured-coverage\n44|  subsection untouched), `LOGBOOK.md` (newest-first entry)\n45|- `internal/traceability` untouched (final leaf owns registry bindings + re-pin)\n46|- `task-board.config.json` == HEAD (restored by hand after refresh; the trunk\n47|  race-gate fix is taken, not forked)\n48|\n49|## Test evidence (all exits real, logs in the evidence tar)\n50|\n51|Rev1 run (RUN-260917-b15a5b):\n52|\n53|- `go test ./internal/meshneg -count=1 -v` → ok, 15/15 tests pass\n54|- `go test ./internal/meshneg -race -count=1 -cover` → ok, 87.8% statements\n55|- Mutants: `PYTHONDONTWRITE