{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7db","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0cd-d72e-7f30-ae43-709d74382df9"},"sequence":584,"recorded_at":1780531400001163,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0cef41070ae80fd6614a74b39ab","text":"Read text file `.temp/resources/TASK-260830-219okr/TASK-260830-219okr_conformance-matrix.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-219okr conformance matrix — dual-stack major negotiation\n2|\n3|Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md` (commit `0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`),\n4|Sections 6.4/6.5/6.6, 11.2-11.3, 11.8, 11.9, 11.10.1, 15.1-15.3, 17.1-17.4.\n5|Historical scope: SPEC v0.5.0, Sections 11.2-11.3 and 17 (unchanged behavior retained).\n6|\n7|Coverage: **11 of 11 AC rows driven** through production entries by named committed tests.\n8|Production package: `internal/meshneg` (`negotiate.go`).\n9|\n10|| # | AC row | Pinned clauses | Production call site | Named test(s) | Verdict |\n11|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n12|| 1 | Negotiate supported majors: highest common major for legacy generations; Config-4 selects RPC 5 | 6.4, 6.5, 6.6, 11.8, 11.9, 11.10.1, 17.1 | `meshneg.Negotiate` via `LocalMajors`, `PeerOffer`, `Select` | `TestNegotiateMatrix` (16 generation-x-major pairs), `TestSelectHighestCommon` admit-*, `TestLocalMajors` | PASS |\n13|| 2 | Preserve core-only peers: v2 negotiation performs core sync only, no major coercion | 11.8, 11.9, 17.1 | `meshneg.Negotiate`, `meshneg.PeerOffer` | `TestNegotiateMatrix` (`*-x-2.0.0`), `TestSemverAgreementWithRPCWire` other-major-* (decode admits syntax, negotiation refuses coercion) | PASS |\n14|| 3 | Expose unsupported directory activation as `directory_mesh_unsupported`, never zero inventory | 11.8, 15.3 (1.2.0 exit-6 row) | `meshneg.Negotiate` → `Decision.Peer.Directory` | `TestPeerExposure`, `TestExposureCarriesNoInventory`, `TestRefusalClassesResolveFromTheRegistry` | PASS |\n15|| 4 | Expose unsupported backend activation with the RPC-4 equivalent (`terminal_backend_unavailable`), never empty | 11.9, 15.3 (1.3.0 exit-6 row), 17.4 | `meshneg.Negotiate` → `Decision.Peer.BackendEvidence` | `TestPeerExposure`, `TestExposureCarriesNoInventory`, `TestRefusalClassesResolveFromTheRegistry` | PASS |\n16|| 5 | Refuse no-common-major with `incompatible_protocol`/exit 6, only when incompatibility is actually known; unknown local config refuses `invalid_config`/exit 3 | 11.2, 11.10.1, 15.1, 15.3, 6.6 | `meshneg.Negotiate`/`Select`/`LocalMajors` → `*meshneg.Refusal` | `TestNegotiateMatrix` (refusal pairs), `TestSelectHighestCommon` refuse-*, `TestLocalMajors` unknown-*, `TestRefusalShape`, `TestRefusalClassesResolveFromTheRegistry` | PASS |\n17|| 6 | Config-4 endpoint never downgrades below RPC 5 and refuses every legacy frame | 6.6, 11.10.1 | `meshneg.LocalMajors`, `meshneg.Negotiate` | `TestConfig4NeverDowngrades` | PASS |\n18|| 7 | Legacy installation offered RPC-5-only refuses instead of coercing | 11.8, 11.9, 17.1 | `meshneg.Negotiate` | `TestLegacyNeverSelectsRPC5` | PASS |\n19|| 8 | Refuse cross-major mixing: mixed rpc arrays, frame/offer disagreement, v2 bound inside v3+ frame | 11.2, 11.8, 11.9, 17.1, 17.2 | `meshneg.PeerOffer` | `TestPeerOfferRefusals` (frame-versions, shape, mixed), `TestSemverAgreementWithRPCWire` | PASS |\n20|| 9 | No byte sniffing, extension field, argv value, environment value, or failed handshake selects a fallback | 6.6 | `meshneg.Negotiate` (no such input exists) | `TestNoFallbackSurface` (environment, argv, stateless, extension-member) | PASS |\n21|| 10 | Exact per-major shapes: 14/24/25/25 contract keys, 6/7/8/8 namespaces, bound Structured Error 1.0.0/1.2.0/1.3.0/1.3.0; RPC 5 carries exact RPC-4 shapes | 11.2, 11.8, 11.9, 11.10.1, 15.1, 15.3 | `meshneg.Negotiate` → `Decision` via `rpcwire.ContractProfile`, `rpcwire.Namespaces`, `axerror.BindingFor` | `TestDecisionShapes` | PASS |\n22|| 11 | Negotiation never substitutes admission and advertises no capability: identity/allowlist/generation ignored; outcomes pure data | 11.10.1, 6.6 | `meshneg.Negotiate` (ignores identity-adjacent members) | `TestNegotiationIsNotAdmission`, `TestNegotiationIsDeterministic`, `TestExposureCarriesNoInventory` | PASS |\n23|\n24|## Negative-test inventory (every refusal gate)\n25|\n26|| Gate (production site) | Rejected class | Named negative test | Narrowing mutant (killed) |\n27|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n28|| `LocalMajors` Config-1 row | majors 3, 4, 5 for Config-1 | `TestNegotiateMatrix/1.0.0-x-3.0.0` | `config1-admits-3` |\n29|| `LocalMajors` Config-2 row | majors 4, 5 for Config-2 | `TestNegotiateMatrix/2.0.0-x-4.0.0` | `config2-admits-4` |\n30|| `LocalMajors` Config-3 row | major 5 for Config-3 | `TestNegotiateMatrix/3.0.0-x-5.0.0` | `config3-admits-5` |\n31|| `LocalMajors` Config-4 row | majors 2, 3, 4 for Config-4 | `TestConfig4NeverDowngrades` | `config4-admits-4` |\n32|| `LocalMajors` default | any generation outside 1.0.0-4.0.0 | `TestLocalMajors/unknown-9.9.9` | `unknown-config-admits-9` |\n33|| `PeerOffer` frame vocabulary | versions outside pinned 2.0.0-5.0.0 | `TestPeerOfferRefusals/frame-versions` | `frame-admits-2.1` |\n34|| `PeerOffer` contracts key count | extra keys (incl. extensions) | `TestPeerOfferRefusals/shape/extra-error-key`, `TestNoFallbackSurface/extension-member` | `shape-admits-extra-key` |\n35|| `PeerOffer` contracts key membership | substituted keys at equal count | `TestPeerOfferRefusals/shape/substituted-key` | `shape-admits-missing-lease` |\n36|| `PeerOffer` rpc array length | empty and 17-entry arrays | `TestPeerOfferRefusals/shape/empty-rpc`, `.../seventeen-rpc` | `rpc-admits-nil-empty`, `rpc-admits-17` |\n37|| `PeerOffer` rpc major agreement | mixed majors, cross-major frames | `TestPeerOfferRefusals/mixed/*` | `mixed-admits-v3-in-v2`, `mixed-admits-v-prefix-value` |\n38|| `PeerOffer` rpc version grammar | non-semver versions | `TestPeerOfferRefusals/mixed/not-semver`, `TestSemverAgreementWithRPCWire` | `semver-admits-v-prefix`, `major-extract-plus-one` (token-preserving) |\n39|| `PeerOffer` rpc sort order | duplicate/unsorted arrays | `TestPeerOfferRefusals/mixed/unsorted` | `mixed-admits-unsorted-pair` |\n40|| `PeerOffer` v3+ exactness | inexact v3/v4/v5 rpc arrays | `TestPeerOfferRefusals/shape/v3-inexact-rpc` | `v3-exact-admits-3.0.1` |\n41|| `Select` input vocabulary | majors outside 2/3/4/5 on either side | `TestSelectHighestCommon/refuse-local-names-6`, `refuse-peer-mixes-1-with-common` | `select-admits-local-6`, `select-admits-peer-1` |\n42|| `Select` highest-common rule | non-highest selection | `TestSelectHighestCommon/admit-highest-wins` | `select-picks-lowest` |\n43|| `Select` disjoint refusal | disjoint offer pairs | `TestSelectHighestCommon/refuse-disjoint` | `select-admits-disjoint-2v3` |\n44|| `decisionFor` directory threshold | directory negotiated below major 3 | `TestPeerExposure/2.0.0` | `exposure-directory-at-2` |\n45|| `decisionFor` backend threshold | backend negotiated below major 4 | `TestPeerExposure/3.0.0` | `exposure-backend-at-3` |\n46|| `decisionFor` error binding | wrong containing contract | `TestDecisionShapes/3.0.0` | `error-binding-provider-contract` |\n47|| `refuse` refusal class | wrong Section 15 code | `TestNegotiateMatrix/3.0.0-x-5.0.0` | `refusal-code-transport-failure` |\n48|| `exposure` version pins | wrong introducing Error version | `TestPeerExposure/2.0.0` | `directory-version-1.0.0`, `backend-version-1.2.0` |\n49|| `shapeRefusal` reason | misreported reason | `TestPeerOfferRefusals/shape/extra-error-key` | `reason-shape-reports-mixed` |\n50|\n51|Harness: `internal/meshneg/mutations.py` (27 narrowing probes, all killed; neutral passed;\n52|`detail-text` harmless control survived as designed). Per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits,\n53|and mutant table under `.temp/TASK-260830-219okr/mutations-meshneg/`, archived in the\n54|producer evidence tar. (Rev1 text said \"28\"; the harness defines 29 probes total =\n55|27 narrowing + neutral + harmless control. Re-executed exit 0 by successor run\n56|RUN-260917-244f06; tallied from `results.json`, not the prose.)\n57|\n58|## Stated bounds\n59|\n60|- Within-major minor selection for v2 1-16 rpc ranges is not performed; any 2.x range\n61|  selects major 2 (`TestPeerOfferRefusals/admitted-ranges`).\n62|- Handshake sequencing (hello-first, request_id echo, one framed refusal then close) stays\n63|  with rpcwire decode plus the connection responder; `Negotiate` takes decoded hellos.\n64|- Admission (identity equality, allowlist, trust generation) stays with TASK-260830-z1yxg9;\n65|  separation is pinned by `TestNegotiationIsNotAdmission`.\n66|- No durable state is written; crash/idempotency surface is absent by construction\n67|  (direct imports exclude os/io/net/time/rand/exec; owners consulted through pure\n68|  functions only; `TestNegotiationIsDeterministic` pins statelessness).\n69|- Traceability registry bindings and digest re-pin belong to the story final leaf; clause\n70|  coverage lives in `internal/meshneg/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n71|- No `ax` command, doctor result, or runtime capability is claimed anywhere in this leaf.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
