{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d7a3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0cd-d72e-7f30-ae43-709d74382df9"},"sequence":2604,"recorded_at":1780531400005203,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"02a966f3-4024-4d79-8d10-466a4e1198b3"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review.\n\nRework-rev4 for TASK-260830-219okr answers all six rev3 findings (3×P2, 3×P3) as evidence + documentation, with zero production selection-logic change:\n\n- **F1**: exposure expectations now assert the literal `directory_mesh_unsupported` / `terminal_backend_unavailable` tokens at the `Negotiate` entry; no committed test derives from the production constants. Two same-exit swap plants added, both killed by `TestPeerExposure/2.0.0`.\n- **F2**: new `TestNegotiateUnknownGeneration` drives 8 unknown generations × 4 frames through `Negotiate` (code/exit/reason/sentinel + zero `Decision`); the Negotiate-site fallback plant is killed by it.\n- **F3**: docs name `LoadedConfiguration.SourceVersion` (not the normalized `SchemaVersion`); new `TestLocalMajorsTracksConfigVocabulary` pins the mapping against the config constants with a Decode-level normalization proof.\n- **F4**: stated-bound option — non-`rpc` arrays validated by rpcwire decode, trusted here; pinned by `TestPeerOfferTrustsDecodedNonRPCArrays`. My probe showed v2 `lease=[\"9.9.9\"]` is admitted by decode too (valid range by design, not a hole).\n- **F5**: frame rows `4.1.0`/`5.0.1`/`5.1.0` + 5.x-edge plant (killed) + unparseable-class bound stated.\n- **F6**: TRACEABILITY 17.1 minor clause dropped.\n\nVerification (all observed exits): 18/18 package tests green, mutant harness exit 0 with 31 narrowing killed / neutral passed / harmless control